<!-- 10 Trust -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="kicker">Solution &middot; trust &amp; compliance</div>
  <h1>Designed for auditors, not just for demos</h1>
  <div class="grid2" style="margin-top:16px">
    <div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Irreversible redaction</h3><p>Boxes are burned into the page pixels and the exported PDF has no text layer &mdash;
        nothing to copy-paste from under a black rectangle, the most common real-world redaction failure.</p></div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:12px"><h3>Human in the loop &mdash; and a safety net</h3><p>Every finding shows its source (RULE / LLM / VLM), confidence, role and reason;
        the reviewer accepts or rejects each box. An <b>unread-ink check</b> flags any text-like region the OCR did not read, so a page never passes silently.</p></div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:12px"><h3>Tamper-evident audit</h3><p>Ingest, detection, review, policy change and export events are appended to a SHA-256
        hash chain. Editing or deleting any record breaks verification. Documents themselves are never logged &mdash; only their hashes.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card" style="background:#fff"><h3>Open, commercially usable components</h3>
        <table class="t" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:13px">
          <tr><th>Component</th><th>Role</th><th>License</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Qwen3 (8B / 30B-A3B)</td><td>contextual LLM</td><td>Apache-2.0</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Qwen2.5-VL-7B</td><td>vision-language</td><td>Apache-2.0</td></tr>
          <tr><td>PP-OCR via RapidOCR</td><td>OCR</td><td>Apache-2.0</td></tr>
          <tr><td>FastAPI, pypdfium2, OpenCV</td><td>server, PDF, vision</td><td>MIT / Apache / BSD</td></tr>
          <tr><td>vLLM (XPU)</td><td>B70 serving</td><td>Apache-2.0</td></tr>
          <tr><td>RedactAgent (this work)</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>MIT</td></tr>
        </table>
        <p class="note" style="margin-top:8px">No AGPL detectors (e.g. Ultralytics YOLO) &mdash; deliberately chosen so the
          organisers and customers can use the work commercially.</p></div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:12px"><h3>All test data is synthetic</h3><p>Every name, ID and address in this proposal was generated
        (with valid checksums) &mdash; no real personal data was used to build or evaluate RedactAgent.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><span>RedactAgent &middot; ASUS UGen AI League 2026</span><span>10</span></div>
</section>
